{% if spec.has("websockets") %}

## WebSockets

The `/ws` endpoint echoes every text message it receives:

```python
from websockets.sync.client import connect

with connect("ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws") as websocket:
    websocket.send("hello")
    print(websocket.recv())
```
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("rate-limit") %}

## Rate limiting

The application installs a SlowAPI limiter as `app.state.limiter` with a default
limit of 100 requests per minute. The `/limited` endpoint demonstrates a tighter
limit of 5 requests per minute. Exceeding a limit returns `429` with a JSON
`detail` field.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("sentry") %}

## Error reporting

Sentry is initialized at startup only when `SENTRY_DSN` is set. Leave it empty to
disable reporting. `SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT` controls the environment label.
{% endif %}
